    "text": {
     "en": "Every number greater than 1 can be written as a product of primes. This is prime factorisation. 12 is 2 times 2 times 3.\nWe can use a factor tree: split a number into two factors and keep splitting until all are prime.\nThe prime factorisation of a number is unique apart from order."
    }
